A quick hint for those of you who want to play both on Linux console and
X11, and don't like the idea of always editing your .nethackrc to change
between windowtype:x11 and windowtype:tty, and whatever you may wish to
have different between console and X11.

Add these lines to the /usr/games/nethack script somewhere so that they
are executed before starting the actual game:

if [ "$TERM" == xterm  -a  -f $HOME/.nethackrc.x11 ] ; then
     NETHACKOPTIONS=$HOME/.nethackrc.x11
fi

Then, copy your .nethackrc as .nethackrc.x11.
Your settings will be read from .nethackrc.x11 when you start the game
from xterm and the file exists, and otherwise .nethackrc will be used as
before, so put your console preferences in .nethackrc and x11 preferences
in .nethackrc.x11.

If you use an icon in X11 to start the game, you will probably need to
check the "Run in terminal" box in the launcher properties. (At least my
computer didn't want to launch the game from an icon before that. Or is
there something else I didn't know about this?)

And before you compile the game after that, you'll probably want to add
the same lines to sys/unix/nethack.sh in the source tree, because that is
used as a template to overwrite the script when you install or update the
game. 

